<div class="tt-leadership-page"><section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-grid"><div><p class="kicker">PCM Leadership Training</p><h1>Understand<br class="tt-vtablet-h1-first-break"> different people<span class="tt-h1-punct">.</span> <span class="tt-h1-lead">Lead</span><br class="tt-vtablet-h1-break"> with more choice.</h1><p class="lead"><span class="tt-hero-line">A practical 16-hour Process Communication Model® programme for leaders</span> <span class="tt-hero-line">who want to understand what motivates different people, recognise stress earlier</span> <span class="tt-hero-line">and adapt communication to real people and real situations.</span></p><div class="meta meta-stacked">
  <div class="meta-row"><span>16 hours</span><span class="dot">·</span><span>Personal Leadership Profile</span><span class="dot">·</span><span>In person</span></div>
  <div class="meta-row"><span>ET</span><span class="dot">·</span><span>EN</span><span class="dot">·</span><span>RU</span></div>
</div><a class="btn" href="https://calendly.com/tujutaju/free-pcm-intro-call">Book a 20-minute introduction call</a></div><div class="hero-art" aria-label="Abstract leadership visual about communication, motivation and stress"><img width="576" height="640" src="https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Leadership_tujutaju_metallic.webp" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-2873" alt="leadership tujutaju metallic" decoding="async" srcset="https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Leadership_tujutaju_metallic.webp 576w, https://tujutaju.ee/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Leadership_tujutaju_metallic-270x300.webp 270w" sizes="(max-width: 576px) 100vw, 576px" /></div></div></section>

<section class="blue-band"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><p class="kicker">Leadership through PCM</p><h2>Different people need different ways of being led.</h2></div><div class="leadership-copy">
  <p>PCM gives leaders a practical framework for understanding personality differences, psychological needs, motivation and behaviour under stress.</p>
  <p>It also starts with the leader: understanding your own strengths, preferred ways of leading, reactions under stress and patterns you may not notice as quickly in yourself.</p>
  <p>The goal is not to learn one “correct” leadership style, but to recognise what is happening — in yourself and in others — and choose a way of communicating that fits the person and the situation.</p>
</div></div></section>

<section><div class="wrap"><p class="kicker">What participants learn</p><h2>From understanding people to leading them more consciously</h2><div class="learn-grid">
<div class="learn-item"><h3>Recognise people faster</h3><p>Notice communication clues, personality preferences and the first signs that contact is becoming more difficult.</p></div>
<div class="learn-item"><h3>Motivate more precisely</h3><p>Understand different psychological needs and choose ways of communicating that support motivation and engagement.</p></div>
<div class="learn-item"><h3>Return communication to a constructive track</h3><p>Recognise early stress and misunderstanding, adapt your approach and reduce the risk of escalation.</p></div>
<div class="learn-item"><h3>Understand yourself as a leader</h3><p>See your own strengths, preferred leadership patterns, stress responses and ways to stay more effective in difficult situations.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="profile"><div class="wrap profile-grid"><div><p class="kicker">Your Leadership Profile</p><h2>Your own communication is part of the leadership system.</h2></div><div class="profile-editorial"><p>Before the training, each participant completes the official PCM questionnaire and receives a personal Leadership Profile. It connects the model directly to your own communication, motivation, interaction preferences and patterns under stress.</p><div class="profile-list editorial-list"><div><strong>Personality Structure & strengths</strong></div><div><strong>Communication & interaction preferences</strong></div><div><strong>Psychological needs & motivation</strong></div><div><strong>Stress patterns & practical reflection</strong></div></div></div></div></section>

<section><div class="wrap"><p class="kicker">How the training works</p><h2>Learn it. Notice it. Try it in real life.</h2><div class="process-grid process-five">
<div class="step"><div class="n">01</div><h3>Profile</h3><p>Start with your personal PCM Leadership Profile.</p></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">02</div><h3>Understand</h3><p>Build a shared language for personality, motivation and stress.</p></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">03</div><h3>Practise</h3><p>Work individually, in pairs and in groups with practical exercises and cases.</p></div>
<div class="step"><div class="n">04</div><h3>Apply</h3><p>Use the time between sessions to notice patterns in everyday work and try new approaches in real situations.</p></div>
<div class="step follow-up"><div class="n">05</div><h3>Follow up</h3><p>Meet again after the training to discuss what happened in practice, ask questions and refine how PCM is used in everyday work.</p></div>
</div><p class="follow-note">The goal is not to finish the training and leave the profile on a shelf. Follow-up helps turn PCM into an everyday working tool.</p></div></section>

<section class="school"><div class="wrap school-grid"><div><p class="kicker">For schools & education</p><h2>A teacher is a leader, too.</h2><p class="school-note">PCM Leadership Training can be used in schools for teachers and school leaders, without turning it into a separate “school version” of the model.</p></div><div class="school-copy"><p>A teacher leads every day: creates a frame, guides learning, motivates, keeps a group together and adapts communication to different people and situations.</p><p>PCM gives schools a shared language for understanding what motivates different students, how they take in information, how stress changes behaviour and communication, and what can help restore contact.</p><p>For experienced teachers, much of this may already happen intuitively. PCM helps make that knowledge more conscious, easier to discuss and easier to use consistently across a school team.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="format"><div class="wrap format-grid"><div><p class="kicker">Format</p><h2>16 hours with time to apply what you learn</h2></div><div class="facts">
<div class="fact"><strong>4 × 4 hours</strong><span>Four meetings with space between them for real-life observation and practice.</span></div>
<div class="fact"><strong>In person</strong><span>For organisations, teams and schools.</span></div>
<div class="fact"><strong>ET · EN · RU</strong><span>The training can be delivered in Estonian, English or Russian.</span></div>
<div class="fact"><strong>Practical by design</strong><span>Theory, individual work, pair/group exercises, video analysis and real group cases.</span></div>
</div></div></section>

<section><div class="wrap"><p class="kicker">What changes after the training</p><h2>More options in the moments that matter</h2><div class="outcomes-grid">
<div class="outcome"><h3>Clearer communication</h3><p>More choice in how you explain, direct, give feedback and build trust with different people.</p></div>
<div class="outcome"><h3>Earlier recognition of stress</h3><p>Notice when communication starts to move off track and respond before tension grows.</p></div>
<div class="outcome"><h3>More conscious motivation</h3><p>Understand what different people need in order to stay engaged, resourceful and able to contribute.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="cta"><div class="wrap"><div class="cta-panel"><div><h2>Bring a shared language<br class="tt-desktop-cta-break"> for leadership<br class="tt-desktop-cta-break"> to your organisation.</h2></div><div class="cta-right"><p>Tell me about your team, organisation or school. We can look at the context and choose the right way to run the training.</p><a class="btn" href="https://calendly.com/tujutaju/free-pcm-intro-call">Book a 20-minute introduction call</a></div></div></div></section></div><style id="tt-normalize-20261006-2864">.tt-leadership-page .hero .kicker{font-family:Poppins,sans-serif!important;font-size:18px!important;font-weight:700!important;line-height:1.3!important;letter-spacing:.12em!important;text-transform:uppercase!important;margin:0!important}.tt-leadership-page .hero h1{margin:19px 0 0!important}.tt-leadership-page .hero .lead{margin-top:12px!important}.tt-leadership-page .cta h2{color:var(--blue,#626E98)!important}.tt-leadership-page .btn{border-radius:16px 0 16px 16px!important}@media(max-width:620px){.tt-leadership-page .hero-grid>div:first-child{text-align:right!important}}</style>
